From c4957820d82d20c054ee982efd819405b686e530 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:25:45 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(post): the Tormach safe retract comes from the
 machine file

G53 G0 Z0 is straight up only where machine Z0 is the top of Z travel
(Tormach's convention); a LinuxCNC machine homed with Z0 at the bottom
rapids down into the part. The .mch Z part now states `safe_retract`
(machine coordinates, file unit; mirrored as `safeRetractZ`, mm), every
shipped Tormach file and the generic VMCs state 0, and tormach.cps
retracts to the stated Z. A document with no machine or a Tormach model
stating none keeps Z0 + G30 byte-identical; any other machine stating
none is refused by name. A non-zero safe Z drops the PathPilot G30 (an
unset G30 position is the machine origin) and says so in the header.

Fixes #495

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
